---
// Self-hosted AI coding agent comparison page (DVN-3.1). Targets the broader
// "self-hosted AI coding agent" query — the fully-in-your-cloud vs hybrid
// architecture split is the sorting criterion. Every competitor claim below
// is sourced from goals/drafts/devin-alternative-positioning-research.md's
// safe-to-print register (2026-07-14), re-verified against vendor primary
// sources on 2026-10-02 (Cursor and Factory rows updated) and again on 2026-11-02
// (Factory, OpenHands and Cursor rows updated), and cited inline.
// Re-verify before any future edit — see brand/MESSAGING.md D10 for the surface-scoped
// competitor-naming policy this page operates under. OpenCode is
// deliberately not named (unverified — never-print list).
// The compliance FAQ (SAUL-SHF-1.1) is sourced from
// site/src/content/docs/security.mdx and must stay consistent with it.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ComparisonTable from "../components/ComparisonTable.astro";
import TryItCta from "../components/TryItCta.astro";
import { escapeHtml } from "../lib/html-escape";

const verifiedDate = "November 2, 2026";

// Sources (Appendix, devin-alternative-positioning-research.md).
const src = {
  cursor: "https://cursor.com/changelog/self-hosted-machines",
  cursorSelfHosted: "https://cursor.com/docs/cloud-agent/self-hosted",
  cursorAgentSdk: "https://cursor.com/docs/agent-sdk/deployment",
  openhandsPricing: "https://www.openhands.dev/pricing",
  openhandsLicense: "https://github.com/OpenHands/OpenHands/blob/main/LICENSE",
  openhandsEnterprise: "https://github.com/OpenHands/enterprise",
  coder: "https://coder.com/docs",
  devinDeployment: "https://docs.devin.ai/enterprise/deployment/overview",
  devinReleaseNotes: "https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026",
  factoryDeployment: "https://docs.factory.com/enterprise/network-and-deployment",
  factoryPrivate: "https://factory.com/news/factory-private",
  factoryAirgap: "https://docs.factory.com/enterprise/airgapped-deployment",
  factoryPricing: "https://factory.com/pricing",
};

// Compliance FAQ — rendered as HTML and as FAQPage JSON-LD from this one
// array so the two can't drift. No certification claims beyond "SOC 2: no".
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Can Shipwright run inside our private VPC?",
    a: "Yes. The admin service, task store, metrics and agent runtime deploy to infrastructure you own, with Docker or the Helm chart on your own Kubernetes cluster. Your repository and the agent's working copy stay there. By default every service is reachable only inside the cluster.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does any data leave our infrastructure?",
    a: "Yes, the model calls. Shipwright runs Claude Code, which sends prompts and the code context it needs to Anthropic's API on your own API key or Claude account. Agents also reach the services you connect, such as GitHub and Slack. Nothing goes to Shipwright or App Vitals, because there is no Shipwright-hosted service in the path.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can several agents run at once, isolated from each other?",
    a: "Yes. On Kubernetes each agent gets its own Deployment, persistent volume, Secret and scoped token. Self-serve tenant agent pods can be isolated with an opt-in NetworkPolicy (off by default, and enforced only if your CNI supports NetworkPolicy) that allows DNS, the Shipwright services and the public internet. For other agents, egress restriction is your own NetworkPolicy or firewall rules.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is Shipwright SOC 2 certified?",
    a: "No, not currently. Shipwright is MIT-licensed software you run, not a hosted service, so it runs under your own controls. A fully egress-locked or air-gapped deployment isn't supported out of the box, because agents need to reach the model API.",
  },
];

const faqLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqs.map(({ q, a }) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: a },
  })),
};

const architectureRows = [
  {
    tool: "Shipwright",
    license: "MIT",
    architecture: "Fully in your own cloud — control plane included.",
    detail:
      "The admin, metrics, and agent runtime all deploy to infrastructure you own (Docker or your own Kubernetes cluster). No managed service sits between your repository and the agent.",
    citation: null,
    self: true,
  },
  {
    tool: "Cursor (self-hosted cloud agents)",
    license: "Proprietary",
    architecture: "Hybrid — no documented customer-controlled control plane.",
    detail:
      "Self-hosted machines keep your codebase, build outputs and secrets on your own infrastructure, and the agent runs tool calls there, but Cursor runs the agent loop, inference and planning. Its Agent SDK can be self-hosted, yet still signs in to Cursor's API. No spec phase, no deploy stage.",
    citation: [src.cursor, src.cursorSelfHosted, src.cursorAgentSdk],
    self: false,
  },
  {
    tool: "OpenHands",
    license: "MIT (Agent Canvas); commercial server in a separate repo under a PolyForm free-trial licence",
    architecture: "Multi-user self-host is a paid commercial offering.",
    detail:
      "The open-source Agent Canvas is MIT and free to self-host on a laptop or shared VM, automations and isolated Docker runtimes included. Multi-user identity, role-based access control and SSO for a self-hosted install are part of the vendor's paid commercial offering.",
    citation: [src.openhandsPricing, src.openhandsLicense, src.openhandsEnterprise],
    self: false,
  },
  {
    tool: "Coder Agents",
    license: "Governance platform, not an OSS agent",
    architecture: "No built-in cloud runtime to compare — it wraps agents you run.",
    detail:
      "Scope stops at code, tests, and PRs. No spec phase, no deploy stage, no built-in cron.",
    citation: src.coder,
    self: false,
  },
  {
    tool: "Devin",
    license: "Proprietary",
    architecture: "Cognition-hosted control plane at every tier.",
    detail:
      "Devin Outposts can run the execution sandbox in your own environment, but the agent loop — the brain — always resides in Cognition's cloud. Full breakdown at /vs/devin.",
    citation: [src.devinDeployment, src.devinReleaseNotes],
    self: false,
  },
  {
    tool: "Factory",
    license: "Proprietary",
    architecture: "Cloud-orchestrated by default — running it yourself is sales-gated.",
    detail:
      "Factory Managed keeps the control plane in Factory's cloud. Factory Private, launched September 2026 and in private preview by request, runs Droid sandboxes in your VPC, but Factory still hosts the control plane by default. Only a Custom Deployment, airgapped builds included, puts all of Factory inside your network, and both go through Factory's sales team with no self-serve path.",
    citation: [src.factoryDeployment, src.factoryPrivate, src.factoryAirgap, src.factoryPricing],
    self: false,
  },
];

// ComparisonTable props for the architecture table. Header/cell style
// strings are reproduced exactly from the original hand-copied <table>
// markup.
const architectureColumns = [
  {
    label: "Tool",
    style: "text-align:left; padding:0.6rem 1rem 0.6rem 0; font-family:var(--sw-font-mono); font-size:0.8125rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; color:var(--sw-color-text-muted); white-space:nowrap;",
  },
  {
    label: "License",
    style: "text-align:left; padding:0.6rem 1rem; font-family:var(--sw-font-mono); font-size:0.8125rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; color:var(--sw-color-text-muted); white-space:nowrap;",
  },
  {
    label: "Architecture",
    style: "text-align:left; padding:0.6rem 1rem; font-family:var(--sw-font-mono); font-size:0.8125rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; color:var(--sw-color-text-muted); white-space:nowrap;",
  },
];

const architectureTableRows = architectureRows.map((row) => {
  const citations = Array.isArray(row.citation)
    ? row.citation
    : row.citation
      ? [row.citation]
      : [];
  const sourceLinks = citations
    .map((c) => `<a href="${c}" class="text-sm">\n[source]\n</a>`)
    .join("  ");
  return {
    highlight: row.self,
    cells: [
      {
        style: "padding:0.9rem 1rem 0.9rem 0; vertical-align:top;",
        html: `<span style="font-family:var(--sw-font-display); font-weight:600; color:${row.self ? "var(--sw-color-brand-default)" : "var(--sw-color-text-heading)"};"> ${escapeHtml(row.tool)} </span>`,
      },
      {
        style: "padding:0.9rem 1rem; vertical-align:top; color:var(--sw-color-text-body);",
        html: ` ${escapeHtml(row.license)} `,
      },
      {
        style: "padding:0.9rem 1rem 0.9rem 1rem; vertical-align:top; color:var(--sw-color-text-body);",
        html: sourceLinks
          ? ` <strong>${escapeHtml(row.architecture)}</strong> <span> ${escapeHtml(row.detail)}</span>  ${sourceLinks}  `
          : ` <strong>${escapeHtml(row.architecture)}</strong> <span> ${escapeHtml(row.detail)}</span>  `,
      },
    ],
  };
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Self-hosted AI coding agent — Shipwright Harness"
  description="Shipwright is a self-hosted AI coding agent: the control plane, agent runtime and your code all run in your own cloud. Model calls go to Anthropic on your own key."
  pagefindIgnore={true}
>
  <!-- Page header -->
  <section class="relative z-10 pt-16 pb-8">
    <p class="sw-label">Comparison</p>
    <h1 class="sw-h1 mt-4 max-w-3xl">
      A <span class="sw-gradient-text">self-hosted</span> AI coding agent —
      entirely in your cloud.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg">
      "Self-hosted" gets used loosely. The real question is architectural:
      does the whole system — control plane included — run on infrastructure
      you own, or does part of it always phone home to someone else's cloud?
      Here is the honest, sourced breakdown.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm" style="color: var(--sw-color-text-muted);">
      Facts verified as of {verifiedDate}, from each vendor's own primary
      sources (linked below). Re-checked immediately before this page ships —
      vendor terms and tiers change.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Architecture comparison table -->
  <section class="relative z-10 pb-16" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--sw-color-border-subtle); padding-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>Fully in your cloud, or hybrid?</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">
      Shipwright's control plane, agent runtime, and your code all run on
      infrastructure you own, at every tier — no managed-service layer in
      between. The rest of the field is either hybrid (part of the system
      stays in the vendor's cloud) or gates full self-hosting behind a
      sales conversation.
    </p>
    <ComparisonTable columns={architectureColumns} rows={architectureTableRows} />
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl sw-editorial">
      "Self-hosted" is table-stakes marketing language across the field now —
      the architecture underneath it is what actually differs. Full head to
      head on Devin specifically: <a href="/vs/devin">/vs/devin →</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Economics — price-free framing (D5). -->
  <section class="relative z-10 pb-16" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--sw-color-border-subtle); padding-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>Economics</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">
      Shipwright: free, MIT, no tiers or seats — the whole pipeline, not a
      gated tier of it. Everyone else in the table above: see each vendor's
      own site for current terms, which change over time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Compliance FAQ (SAUL-SHF-1.1) — consistent with /docs/security. -->
  <section class="relative z-10 pb-16" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--sw-color-border-subtle); padding-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>Questions security and compliance teams ask</h2>
    {faqs.map(({ q, a }) => (
      <>
        <h3 class="mt-8">{q}</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">{a}</p>
      </>
    ))}
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl">
      Deployment model, egress, RBAC, secrets and logging, claim by claim:
      <a href="/docs/security">Security architecture →</a>
    </p>
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(faqLd)} />
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <TryItCta>
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl">
      <a href="/compare">See how Shipwright compares to the rest of the field →</a>
    </p>
  </TryItCta>
</BaseLayout>
